# DO NOT remove this file from git, and do not add it to .gitignore.
#
# It is tracked deliberately. Lovable creates and syncs it, and the deploy expects it to be
# present in the repo — untracking it breaks the Lovable sync and the build.
#
# Everything in here is PUBLIC BY DESIGN:
#   SUPABASE_URL / PROJECT_ID    the project's public endpoint
#   SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY     the anon key, which ships inside the browser bundle anyway
#
# The anon key is not a secret. It identifies the project; it does not authorise anything.
# Access is enforced by Row Level Security on every table plus the SECURITY DEFINER grants —
# see docs/data-model.md and docs/gotchas.md. Verified: the only JWT ever committed to this
# repo is role "anon", and the repo is safe to be public with this file in it.
#
# REAL secrets never go here. They live in:
#   .env.local                   (gitignored by *.local) — SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN
#   the Supabase secret store    — GEMINI_API_KEY, GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD, CRON_SECRET,
#                                  TELEGRAM_*, VAPID_* ... set with `supabase secrets set`
#
# If you are an agent reading this and about to "fix a leaked key": don't. Check the role
# claim first — `has_function_privilege` and get_advisors(type:"security") are the real checks.

